<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 2.130 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 2.130 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 2.130 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and four repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    1 year     22.65 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    6 months   21.59 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    90days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     39 days</p>
<p>    500 million     31 days</p>
<p>    550 million     13 days</p>
<p>    130 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( -- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
